ath of Nadab and Abihu (Lev. 10:12; Num. 3:4) he was appointed to the charge of the sanctuary (Num. 3:32).","verses":61,"father":"Aaron","mother":"Elisheba","v":[1]},{"id":"nun_2214","name":"Nun","also":"Non","summary":"Beyond the fact that he was the father of Joshua nothing more is known of him (Ex. 33:11).","verses":30,"father":"Elishama","mother":"","v":[1]},{"id":"moses_2108","name":"Moses","also":"","summary":"Drawn (or Egypt. mesu, “son;” hence Rameses, royal son). On the invitation of Pharaoh (Gen. 45:17-25), Jacob and his sons went down into Egypt.","verses":774,"father":"Amram","mother":"Jochebed","v":[2,3,5,6,7,9,10,11]},{"id":"joseph_1710","name":"Joseph","also":"Zaphnath-paaneah","summary":"The elder of the two sons of Jacob by Rachel (Gen. 30:23, 24), who, on the occasion of his birth, said, “God hath taken away [Heb. ‘asaph] my reproach.”","verses":199,"father":"Israel","mother":"Rachel","v":[4]},{"id":"ephraim_1206","name":"Ephraim","also":"","summary":"Double fruitfulness (“for God had made him fruitful in the land of his affliction”). The second son of Joseph, born in Egypt (Gen. 41:52; 46:20).","verses":160,"father":"Joseph","mother":"Asenath","v":[4]},{"id":"manasseh_1928","name":"Manasseh","also":"Manasses","summary":"The elder of the two sons of Joseph. He and his brother Ephraim were afterwards adopted by Jacob as his own sons (48:1).","verses":109,"father":"Joseph","mother":"Asenath","v":[4]},{"id":"judah_1751","name":"Judah","also":"","summary":"Praise, the fourth son of Jacob by Leah.","verses":245,"father":"Israel","mother":"Leah","v":[6]},{"id":"caleb_537","name":"Caleb","also":"","summary":"The son of Jephunneh (Num. 13:6; 32:12; Josh. 14:6, 14). He was one of those whom Moses sent to search the land in the second year after the Exodus.","verses":30,"father":"Jephunneh","mother":"","v":[6,13,14]},{"id":"jephunneh_840","name":"Jephunneh","also":"","summary":"The father of Caleb, who was Joshua’s companion in exploring Canaan (Num. 13:6), a Kenezite (Josh. 14:14).","verses":15,"father":"","mother":"","v":[6,13,14]},{"id":"arba_290","name":"Arba","also":"","summary":"","verses":3,"father":"","mother":"","v":[15]}],"places":[{"id":"canaan_272","name":"Canaan","kind":"Region (Country)","lat":31.69353,"lon":34.84388,"summary":"The country which derived its name from the preceding. The name as first used by the Phoenicians denoted only the maritime plain on which Sidon was built.","verses":76,"v":[1]},{"id":"jordan_653","name":"Jordan","kind":"Water (River)","lat":33.18645,"lon":35.61916,"summary":"But besides these two historical fountains there is a third, called the Hasbany, which rises in the bottom of a valley at the western base of Hermon, 12 miles north of Tell-el-Kady.","verses":177,"v":[3]},{"id":"gilgal_476","name":"Gilgal","kind":"City","lat":32.1547,"lon":34.95372,"summary":"From the solemn transaction of the reading of the law in the valley of Shechem between Ebal and Gerizim the Israelites moved forward to Gilgal, and there made a permanent camp (Josh. 9:6; 10:6).","verses":35,"v":[6]},{"id":"kadesh-barnea_663","name":"Kadesh-barnea","kind":"Oasis","lat":30.64805,"lon":34.42261,"summary":"Holy, or Kadesh-Barnea, sacred desert of wandering, a place on the south-eastern border of Palestine, about 165 miles from Horeb. It lay in the “wilderness” or “desert of Zin” (Gen. 14:7; Num. 13:3-26; 14:29-33; 20:1; 27:14), on the border of Edom (20:16).","verses":10,"v":[6,7]},{"id":"hebron_551","name":"Hebron","kind":"City","lat":31.52435,"lon":35.10854,"summary":"A city in the south end of the valley of Eshcol, about midway between Jerusalem and Beersheba, from which it is distant about 20 miles in a straight line.","verses":56,"v":[13,14,15]},{"id":"kiriath-arba_697","name":"Kiriath-arba","kind":"Settlement","lat":31.52435,"lon":35.10854,"summary":"","verses":7,"v":[15]}],"events":[{"id":"dividing_the_land_132","title":"Dividing the land","year":-1445,"summary":"Passage: Joshua 13:1–14:10. People: Jos